# Environment and Docker

The image is the agent's universe. Build it so sealed rollout can run with
`[agent] network_mode = "no-network"`. Runtime model:
`docs/harbor-task-anatomy.md`. Quality bar: `docs/odyssey-quality-guidelines.md`.

## What the Dockerfile must do

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir pytest==8.3.4
WORKDIR /app
COPY app/ /app/
ENV PYTHONPATH=/app
```

- Pin the base tag. Prefer a digest (`@sha256:...`) when you have one; unpinned
  `latest` is forbidden. Odyssey does not require Terminus's canonical ECR list.
- Pin language packages to exact versions. Apt: `--no-install-recommends` and
  clean lists in the same layer. No `apt-get upgrade`.
- `WORKDIR /app`. Copy **only** `app/` (the starting state). Never `COPY tests/`
  or `COPY solution/`. Never `COPY . /app`.
- Bake every dependency the agent, oracle, and verifier need. `test.sh` and
  `solve.sh` must not `pip install`, `npm i`, `apt-get`, `curl`, or `wget`.
- Multi-stage is fine: keep compilers out of the runtime unless the agent must
  compile. Prefer real files plus `COPY` over heredoc-inlined source.

## Harbor reserved paths -- do not create them

The Dockerfile must not `mkdir`, `COPY`, `ADD`, or `chown`:

`/tests` `/solution` `/oracle` `/logs` `/logs/verifier` `/logs/agent`

Harbor mounts those at runtime. Colliding with them fails the trial as infra.

## What must not be in `environment/`

- AI scaffolding: `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `skills.md`, `.cursor/`, `.github/`
  copilot files. The agent should look like a real repo, not an LLM workspace.
- Secrets, `.env`, `.git`, caches, `__pycache__`.
- Held-out fixtures, golden outputs, or a copy of the reference fix.
- Opaque archives extracted in-layer to hide starting-state source.

Spec/docs under `environment/app/` are realistic contracts, not solution guides.

## Runtime network

Image **build** may fetch packages. Agent **rollout** follows
`[agent] network_mode`. `[environment].network_mode` is the Harbor runtime
baseline, not docker-build networking. For a sealed task set environment,
agent, and verifier all to `no-network`. Git clones at build, if any, pin a
commit so later history cannot leak a fix.

## Privileged and compose

No `privileged: true`, no `docker.sock`, no `SYS_ADMIN`. If the objective
truly needs several containers, ship compose and say so in the instruction and
draft; most Odyssey tasks should be one Dockerfile.

## Local check

```bash
docker build -t odyssey-task environment
docker run --rm -it odyssey-task bash
```

Confirm `/app` has the starting state, `tests/` is absent, and the commands
you will put in `solve.sh` actually run.
